    "bodyMarkdown": "# Marketing Campaign Assistant\n\nUse this workflow for broad marketing requests that may touch planning, creative, CRM, lifecycle messaging, or internal updates.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: direct user brief AND at least one requested execution lane.\n\n- Add `notion-mcp` when reading/writing strategy docs, campaign plans, or content calendars.\n- Add `figma-api` only for visual assets or design handoff.\n- Add `google-sheets-mcp` only for campaign trackers, lists, reporting, or lightweight CRM tables.\n- Add `gmail-mcp` only for email drafting/sending from a workspace inbox.\n- Add `customerio-mcp` only for lifecycle messaging, segments, campaigns, or broadcasts.\n- Add `slack-mcp` only for approvals, routing, or delivery.\n- Add `openai-api` only for OpenAI docs/spec lookup, not for normal marketing copy.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nTranslate the user request into lanes first, then install only those lane plugins. If the user says \"full campaign\", select Notion plus the specific requested delivery channels; do not automatically install every marketing plugin.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Classify the request: strategy, copy, SEO, creative, CRM, lifecycle, analytics, or approval.\n2. Pull source material from Notion or Sheets only if selected.\n3. Generate channel-specific deliverables.\n4. Write/update Sheets or lifecycle systems only when explicitly requested.\n5. Create visual assets only when a design lane was selected.\n6. Send Slack approval or summary only if requested.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn deliverables by lane, changed resource URLs, pending approvals, and next actions.",
