    "bodyMarkdown": "# PR Review and Risk Check\n\nUse this workflow to review pull requests and produce an actionable risk assessment.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: (`github-rest-api` OR `git-cli`) AND in-chat review.\n\n- Use `github-rest-api` when fetching PRs, posting comments, adding labels, or reading remote metadata.\n- Use `git-cli` when reviewing local diffs.\n- Add `slack-mcp` only for alerts.\n- Add (`notion-mcp` OR `google-sheets-mcp`) only for review logs/history.\n- Add `openai-api` only for OpenAI docs/spec lookup, not for normal code review reasoning.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nInstall one code source. Add GitHub write access only if comments/labels are requested. Add logging/Slack only when requested.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Fetch PR metadata or local diff.\n2. Identify changed surface area, risky files, migrations, auth/security/data paths, and missing tests.\n3. Produce findings first, with severity and file references.\n4. Score risk and recommend merge/block/follow-up.\n5. Post GitHub comments/labels only if selected.\n6. Log to Notion/Sheets or alert Slack only if selected.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn findings, risk score, test gaps, posted comment/label links, log row/page, and Slack alert link if created.",
