    "bodyMarkdown": "# Analytics to Roadmap\n\nUse this workflow to convert product usage signals into roadmap actions.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: `posthog-mcp` AND (`linear-mcp` OR `notion-mcp` OR in-chat report).\n\n- Require `posthog-mcp` for feature drop-offs, funnels, activation, retention, or event analysis.\n- Add `gmail-mcp` only when the user asks to combine customer feedback or support email context.\n- Use `linear-mcp` for issues or roadmap execution.\n- Use `notion-mcp` for PM briefs or roadmap docs.\n- Use `slack-mcp` only for stakeholder updates.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nInstall PostHog plus the smallest selected destination set. Do not install Gmail unless feedback/support email context is requested.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Identify feature, funnel, cohort, event names, and time window.\n2. Pull PostHog evidence.\n3. Pull Gmail feedback only if selected.\n4. Cluster findings into product problems and opportunities.\n5. Create Linear issues or Notion brief only if selected.\n6. Post Slack summary only if requested.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn metrics, evidence links, user feedback excerpts if used, created issue/doc links, and recommended roadmap actions.",
