    "bodyMarkdown": "# Competitor Brief\n\nUse this workflow to monitor competitor positioning, pages, mentions, and SEO movement.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: (`exa-mcp` OR `tavily-mcp` OR `firecrawl-mcp`) AND in-chat report.\n\n- Use Exa or Tavily for recent mentions, SERP, and market discovery.\n- Use Firecrawl for structured competitor page scraping.\n- Add `ahrefs-mcp` only for SEO metrics, backlinks, keyword movement, or Brand Radar.\n- Add `notion-mcp` only for a durable report.\n- Add `slack-mcp` only for weekly brief delivery or alerts.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nInstall one discovery/crawl lane first. Add Ahrefs/artifact/delivery only when requested by the output.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Identify competitors, market, timeframe, and signal types.\n2. Search or crawl selected competitor pages and mentions.\n3. Pull Ahrefs metrics only if selected; call `doc` before Ahrefs tools.\n4. Summarize positioning changes, feature launches, pricing/page shifts, and SEO changes.\n5. Create Notion report or Slack brief only if selected.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn competitor-by-competitor findings, source URLs, confidence, recommended response, and artifact/message links when created.",
