    "bodyMarkdown": "# Customer Escalation Radar\n\nUse this workflow to detect and route urgent customer issues.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: (`gmail-mcp` OR `slack-mcp` OR `notion-mcp`) AND in-chat escalation report.\n\n- Use Gmail for email escalations.\n- Use Slack for internal/customer channel escalation.\n- Add `google-sheets-mcp` only for customer/account trackers or escalation logs.\n- Add `linear-mcp` only for engineering action items.\n- Add `notion-mcp` only for incident/customer notes.\n- Add Slack as destination only if alerting is requested and Slack is not already selected as source.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nInstall one escalation source first. Add issue/doc/sheet/alert lanes only if requested by the task.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Search selected source for urgent messages by timeframe, customer, severity words, or tags.\n2. Score severity, urgency, revenue/account risk, and owner.\n3. Pull Sheets or Notion context only if selected.\n4. Create Linear/Notion follow-ups only if selected.\n5. Alert Slack only if requested.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn escalation list, source links, severity rationale, recommended owner/action, and created issue/doc/message links.",
