    "bodyMarkdown": "# Design to Shippable UI\n\nUse this workflow to move from design request or design file to implemented UI.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: (`figma-api` OR direct user brief) AND (`github-rest-api` OR `git-cli` OR no code change).\n\n- Use Figma for product/UI design context.\n- Use Figma for marketing/design assets.\n- Use GitHub for repo/PR workflow; use git-cli for local code changes.\n- Add `vercel-api` only for preview deploy.\n- Add `slack-mcp` only for review posting.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nInstall one design/source lane and one code lane only if implementation is requested. Add deploy/review only if requested.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Read design request or fetch design context.\n2. Identify target app, route, components, states, and responsive behavior.\n3. Implement frontend changes when code lane selected.\n4. Open PR or leave local diff based on selected code lane.\n5. Deploy preview only if selected.\n6. Post Slack review only if selected.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn design summary, changed files/PR, preview URL, and Slack review link when created.",
