    "bodyMarkdown": "# Social Content Planner\n\nUse this workflow to create and optionally schedule social content across platforms.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: (`notion-mcp` OR direct user brief) AND in-chat content.\n\n- Use Notion only when content calendar/source docs live there or should be updated.\n- Add `replicate-mcp` only for generated images/video.\n- Add `figma-api` only for editable branded designs.\n- Add `buffer-mcp` only for scheduling/publishing.\n- Add `slack-mcp` only for approval.\n- Add `openai-api` only for OpenAI docs/spec lookup, not for normal post writing.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nSelect content source first, then install media/publishing/approval lanes only if requested.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Parse campaign, audience, platforms, tone, dates, and constraints.\n2. Generate platform-specific posts, hooks, hashtags, CTAs, and alt text.\n3. Generate media or Figma assets only if selected.\n4. Route Slack approval only if selected.\n5. Schedule through Buffer only if selected.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn posts by platform, media/design links, approval status, and scheduled post links.",
