    "bodyMarkdown": "# Release Health Room\n\nUse this workflow during or after a release to correlate deploy health, errors, product metrics, commits, incidents, and stakeholder updates.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: (`sentry-api` OR `posthog-mcp`) AND (`github-rest-api` OR `git-cli`) AND (`slack-mcp` OR `linear-mcp` OR in-chat report).\n\n- Use `sentry-api` for exceptions, traces, releases, and error spikes.\n- Use `posthog-mcp` for funnels, activation, adoption, and event regressions.\n- Use `github-rest-api` for PRs, commits, releases, and remote repo context; use `git-cli` for local checkout correlation.\n- Add `vercel-api` only when deploy status, rollback, or preview URL actions are requested.\n- Add `linear-mcp` only when creating or updating incidents/tasks.\n- Add `slack-mcp` only when posting a release room update.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nInstall the minimum ready set needed by the user's release question. If both Sentry and PostHog are absent, install the one matching the requested signal; ask only when the user asked for both error and product metrics.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Identify release version, deploy window, repository, and environment.\n2. Pull selected health signals from Sentry/PostHog.\n3. Correlate regressions with GitHub or local git commits in the deploy window.\n4. Check Vercel only if deploy/rollback state is needed.\n5. Create or update Linear only if incident tracking is requested.\n6. Post to Slack only if a release-room summary is requested.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn release status, highest-risk regressions, likely commit/PR links, recommended rollback/fix action, incident links, and Slack message link when posted.",
