    "bodyMarkdown": "# Slack Support to Linear Bugs\n\nUse this workflow to turn support messages in Slack into clean engineering issues.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: `slack-mcp` AND `linear-mcp`.\n\n- Require `slack-mcp` for source messages and thread context.\n- Require `linear-mcp` when creating or updating issues.\n- Add `notion-mcp` only for rollups, support digests, or knowledge-base updates.\n- Add `openai-api` only for OpenAI docs/spec lookup, not for classification.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nInstall Slack and Linear. Install Notion only when the user requests a rollup or doc artifact.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Find relevant Slack messages by channel, tag, timeframe, or thread URL.\n2. Classify bug vs support vs feature request.\n3. Extract reproduction steps, expected/actual behavior, affected customer, severity, and evidence links.\n4. Create or update Linear issues.\n5. Write Notion rollup or Slack response only if selected.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn created Linear issue links, source Slack links, severity, owner/team, and rollup link if created.",
