    "bodyMarkdown": "# Spend Anomaly Monitor\n\nUse this workflow to detect unusual spend, duplicate vendors, missing receipts, category spikes, and high-risk transactions.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: (`google-sheets-mcp` OR `ramp-mcp` OR `mercury-mcp`) AND in-chat report.\n\n- Select the finance data source named by the user. If none is named, prefer the installed ready finance source.\n- Add `google-sheets-mcp` when spend data or thresholds live in Sheets, or when the user wants a tracker.\n- Add `slack-mcp` only for approval/review alerts.\n- Add `gmail-mcp` only for email notifications or receipt/invoice follow-up.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nInstall one finance source by default. Add notification plugins only when delivery is requested.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Determine period, threshold, vendor/category dimensions, and source.\n2. Pull transactions or balances from selected finance source.\n3. Compare against baselines, thresholds, duplicates, missing receipts, and unusual vendors.\n4. Write a tracker or alert only if Sheets/Slack/Gmail was selected.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn anomalies with amount, vendor, date, category, reason, recommended owner/action, and notification links when sent.",
