    "bodyMarkdown": "# Lesson to Interactive Site\n\nUse this workflow to turn a video lesson into a shippable interactive page without requiring every design and deploy plugin.\n\n## Minimal gate\n\nDefault path: (`firecrawl-mcp` OR `tavily-mcp` OR provided transcript) AND (`github-rest-api` OR `git-cli`) AND (`vercel-api` OR no deploy).\n\n- Use `firecrawl-mcp` or `tavily-mcp` to extract a transcript/page when no transcript is provided.\n- Add `figma-api` only when visual mockups or editable design assets are requested.\n- Use `github-rest-api` for repo/PR operations; use `git-cli` for local changes.\n- Add Vercel only when a deployed preview is requested.\n- Add `slack-mcp` only for review posting.\n- Add `openai-api` only for OpenAI docs lookup, not for normal lesson summarization.\n\n## Gate protocol\n\nSelect one transcript source, one code path, and one deploy path only if needed. Install/refresh that selected set before Harbor exec.\n\n## Execution\n\n1. Extract or accept the transcript.\n2. Distill learning objectives, sections, examples, and quiz/interaction ideas.\n3. Create the interactive page in the selected repo path.\n4. Add design assets only if the user requested Figma/Figma.\n5. Commit/open PR when GitHub is selected, or leave local changes when `git-cli` is selected.\n6. Deploy preview only if Vercel was selected.\n7. Notify Slack only if requested.\n\n## Final app handoff\n\nBefore finishing, create a Harbor app for the user that exposes the workflow result, report, artifact, or next-action surface behind a Harbor URL. Use workspace-member access by default, and ask for confirmation before publishing anything public.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn lesson outline, changed files or PR URL, preview URL if deployed, and review message link if posted.",
